class:: BeatLoudness
summary:: Beat-synchronous RMS and peak amplitude
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Rhythm
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Onsets2, Classes/BeatTrack3, Classes/BeatBandRatio, Classes/Loudness2

description::
Accumulates squared samples and absolute peaks from one beat edge to the next. Reports the completed interval at the next edge; this is linear signal level, not psychoacoustic loudness or LUFS.

This is an independent implementation of the statistical definition above. Output updates at the server control rate; beat boundaries are quantized to a control block. Silence produces zero level/density or missing tempo evidence. No corpus-level accuracy is implied.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: in
Audio-rate mono signal to measure. Multichannel expansion creates independent analyzers.

argument:: beat
Control-rate beat trigger. Each rising edge completes the preceding interval and begins a new one.

argument:: maxInterval
Maximum beat interval in seconds, clipped to 0.1–60, default 10. Expired results reset to zero.

returns::
[linearRMS, linearPeak], initially zero until a complete beat interval.

examples::
BeatLoudness measures interval-synchronous RMS and peak signal amplitude accumulated between successive beat triggers. In this example, it drives an aggressive sidechain compressor: heavy accented downbeats duck an auxiliary harmonic synth pad, while ghost notes and light hi-hat hits allow the pad to sustain smoothly. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: tracks the interval-synchronous RMS level.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic drum fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
            var kick = SinOsc.ar(EnvGen.ar(Env([120, 45], [0.08], \exp), trig)) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.3), trig);
            var snare = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.15), Impulse.kr(2, 0.5));
            (kick + snare) * 0.5
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, 0.25);
        var onset = Onsets2.kr(chain, threshold: 0.15, fftSize: 1024, hop: 0.25);
        var level = BeatLoudness.kr(source, onset[0], maxInterval: 4.0);
        var rms = level[0].lag(0.04);

        // Sidechain ducking of ambient saw pad
        var pad = Saw.ar([110, 165, 220]).sum * 0.1;
        var duckedPad = pad * (1.0 - (rms * 3.0)).clip(0.05, 1.0);
        var sound = (source * 0.25 ! 2) + duckedPad;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, level[0]) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Beat RMS Level", ~miraBus, 0.0, 0.5);
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
